Lemma 2.2 (Complete recorded evolution). A finite secret-independent tree of complete instruments
and injective gates induces an injective linear map from its root space into the direct sum of its
terminal spaces. For any fixed oracle, an algorithm satisfying the contract has a nonzero total
terminal record.
Proof. At a terminal node use the identity. Induct upward. If the descendant maps Tb are injective,
the composite v 7→(TbLbv)b is injective because the instrument’s combined map is injective. Injective
gates and fixed invertible oracle calls preserve this property. This induction applies separately to
every fixed oracle, including when some individual branches vanish.
